// SDK BRIDGE  -- the only channel out of the sandbox.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The KasVillage SDK itself stays on the native side; the engine holds a thin
// proxy that forwards requests over postMessage and awaits a reply. Three rules
// keep a published scene from doing anything its author should not be able to:
//
//   1. READ-ONLY SURFACE. Nothing fund-moving is reachable. No FROST proposals,
//      no partial signatures, no release txs, no Arweave uploads, no sends. A
//      scene can learn who is playing and what their reputation is; it can
//      never move value or sign anything.
//   2. PERMISSION GATED. The scene declares scene.permissions up front, the
//      native side enforces it, and the player is told what was requested.
//      Undeclared calls are refused by the engine before they even leave.
//   3. NO DIRECT ACCESS. Scene JSON has no verb that calls the SDK. Only the
//      engine invokes it, from node types whose behaviour is fixed here.
